{#-
  Multi-model second-opinion dispatch loop (PLAN-second-opinion-multi-model ADR-011).

  Owns the `config.second_opinion.models` gating so an empty/absent config renders BYTE-ZERO
  (failures.md [fail:design] absent-case rule) — the per-model partials never self-gate.
  For each enabled model, includes the right per-model transport partial (codex / antigravity),
  each of which emits its own invoke + adapt + graceful-skip recipe.

  Callers set `second_opinion_stage` ("review" | "plan") and `is_codex` before the include.
  The `{%- ... %}` whitespace control keeps the disabled render byte-zero.
-#}
{%- set _so = (config.get('second_opinion', {})) if config else {} -%}
{%- set _models = _so.get('models', []) -%}
{%- if _models %}
{% for _m in _models %}
#### Second opinion — model: `{{ _m }}`
{% if _m == 'codex' %}{% include "agents/_partials/second_opinion_codex.md.j2" %}{% elif _m == 'antigravity' %}{% include "agents/_partials/second_opinion_antigravity.md.j2" %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
> **Per-model result contract.** Each enabled model above produces exactly one outcome:
> `status: invoked` (findings adapted + folded in) or `status: skipped`/`failed` (graceful
> degrade, ledger row written). A missing/unauthenticated/rate-limited CLI never blocks the
> stage — it warns and proceeds. Record every model's outcome in `second_opinion_results`.
{%- endif -%}
